# Keep the build context to source only. Two of these are load-bearing:
#  - .env*: the local env file may hold real database credentials; without this
#    line `COPY . .` would bake them into an image layer for anyone with image
#    access to read. Configuration enters the container at RUN time only
#    (see docker-compose.yml's environment block).
#  - node_modules: the host tree is platform-specific (and huge); the image
#    installs its own via `npm ci`. Copying the host's over it would mix
#    Windows/Linux artifacts.
node_modules
.next
generated
.env*
!.env.example
.git
test
playwright-report
test-results
*.tsbuildinfo
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
